FAQs – Artificial Eye Prosthetics in Kalyan

Q1. Does an artificial eye look natural? Modern custom-made acrylic prostheses are painted by skilled ocularists to closely match the fellow eye. Movement is provided by the orbital implant, giving a natural appearance in most cases.

Q2. How long does an artificial eye last? An acrylic prosthesis lasts 5–7 years on average. Children may require replacement more frequently as their socket grows.

Q3. Can an artificial eye be worn while sleeping? Generally, the prosthesis is removed at night to allow socket hygiene and conjunctival rest, though some patients wear it continuously. Your specialist will advise based on your individual socket condition.

Q4. Is there pain involved in wearing a prosthesis? A well-fitted, well-polished prosthesis is comfortable and should not cause pain. Discomfort is a sign of poor fit, surface degradation, or socket infection requiring professional attention.

